    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9b5c9e5c_a7f507d4",
        "filename": "android/soongconfig/modules.go",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 247,
      "author": {
        "id": 1066075
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-11-22T08:27:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "At first I was about to recommend creating collecting the config definitions where one parses the soong.variables, but then I realized that one cannot do that, since the type information is not available there, only the names of the variables :(",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 247,
        "startChar": 36,
        "endLine": 247,
        "endChar": 67
      },
      "revId": "e1c07cfa2bfc223676abb56d7762efaa9ee747cc",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "70263882_3aaa83b5",
        "filename": "android/soongconfig/modules.go",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 248,
      "author": {
        "id": 1066075
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-11-22T08:27:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s kinda odd that you store the config variables in two layers: first you have a slice of Bp2BuildSoongConfigDefinition, then each of those contains slices of variables of different types.\n\nIt would be simpler to have the StringVars/BoolVars/ValueVars slices be a direct member of Config. Is this possible?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 248,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 248,
        "endChar": 38
      },
      "revId": "e1c07cfa2bfc223676abb56d7762efaa9ee747cc",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "05597d2f_3d6ae176",
        "filename": "android/soongconfig/modules.go",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 248,
      "author": {
        "id": 1514900
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-11-22T08:54:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s possible, but this approach keeps soong_config_variables.go simple. I also don\u0027t think it\u0027s simpler/cleaner to flatten the implementation details of config var types into Config as opposed to an abstraction specific for bp2build.",
      "parentUuid": "70263882_3aaa83b5",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 248,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 248,
        "endChar": 38
      },
      "revId": "e1c07cfa2bfc223676abb56d7762efaa9ee747cc",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "59e3a267_97413427",
        "filename": "android/soongconfig/modules.go",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 248,
      "author": {
        "id": 1066075
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-11-22T09:34:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Conceptually, the \"outer\" slice is not how vendor variables work, is it? I thought it\u0027s better if the data in Config reflects the conceptual model instead of just whatever makes the code easier to type.\n\nExample: you are saying that one needs the \"outer\" slice because it keeps soong_config_variables.go simple. True that, but it comes at a cost to whoever looks at Config and it makes modules.go more complicated in turn. It also makes it necessary to add the \"workaround\" Bp2BuildSoongConfigDefinitions type.\n\nInstead, how about this:\n\ntype Bp2BuildSoongConfigDefinitions struct {\n  StringVars map[string][]string,\n  BoolVars: []string,\n  ValueVars: []string,\n}\n\nfunc (*d Bp2BuildSoongConfigDefinition) AddStringVar(...) {\n...}\n\nfunc (*d Bp2BuildSoongConfigDefinition) String() {\n...\n}\n\nThen you don\u0027t have the extra slice, soong_config_variables.go is simple and the concept of \"set of config variables\" is nicely encapsulated.",
      "parentUuid": "05597d2f_3d6ae176",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 248,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 248,
        "endChar": 38
      },
      "revId": "e1c07cfa2bfc223676abb56d7762efaa9ee747cc",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
